stateDiagram-v2
    state "ACTIVE" as available
    state "RETIRED" as retired

    [*] --> available: create preference
    available --> retired: PreferenceLifecycle#retire! / locked reset

    note right of available
      A successful save stores the signed issuance
      and expiry timestamps in the same transaction.
      Chronicle and setting commits are separate.
      Model validation and the reference-table check
      allow only ACTIVE and RETIRED IDs.
    end note

    note right of retired
      The reset transaction also creates a new
      available row. Failed signing rolls back both.
      Reset audit targets the retired row; an audit
      write failure also rolls back the setting work.
      The last issued expiry remains unchanged.
      Its consent receipt remains on the old row;
      the replacement starts without a receipt.
      Cookie emission follows both commit attempts.
      A second retirement is rejected.
      Model validation rejects reactivation.
      The issuance deadline elapses at the last
      expiry plus 30 days; references and holds
      still require separate checks before deletion.
    end note
